    "question": "Nancy has a bag containing 22 tortilla chips. She gives 7 tortilla chips to her brother and 5 tortilla chips to her sister, keeping the rest for herself. How many did Nancy keep for herself?",
    "gold": "10",
    "answer": "She gave away 7+5=<<7+5=12>>12 chips.\nThen she kept 22-12=<<22-12=10>>10.\n#### 10"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many tortilla chips Nancy kept for herself, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Start with the total number of tortilla chips Nancy has initially.\n2. Subtract the number of tortilla chips she gives to her brother.\n3. Subtract the number of tortilla chips she gives to her sister.\n4. The result will be the number of tortilla chips Nancy kept for herself.\n\nLet's go through the calculations step by step:\n\n1. Nancy starts with 22 tortilla chips.\n2. She gives 7 tortilla chips to her brother. So, we subtract 7 from 22:\n   \\[\n   22 - 7 = 15\n   \\]\n3. She then gives 5 tortilla chips to her sister. So, we subtract 5 from 15:\n   \\[\n   15 - 5 = 10\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of tortilla chips Nancy kept for herself is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).",
